<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TO BOOST ELECTRIC 24.9 PCT, GAS 18.8 PCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TO BOOST ELECTRIC 24.9 PCT, GAS 18.8 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hungarian government on Thursday set consumer energy price rises for January 1 at 24.9 percent for electricity and 18.8 percent for gas.</p>
<p>&quot;The review of the energy price increase plan has ended with a good result,&quot; government spokesman Elemer Kiss said after a cabinet meeting. &quot;Electricity prices will go up by 24.9 percent and gas by 18.5 percent.</p>
<p>He added that district heating will rise by 21.9 percent.</p>
</text>
